-- cabal.project for the codegen service.
--
-- Sole purpose right now : relax the `base` upper bound across all deps
-- so that codegen can build against the newest official Haskell Docker
-- image ( haskell:9.14.1-bookworm , which ships base-4.22 ).
--
-- Several of our own upstream packages on Hackage
-- ( dhscanner-ast , dhscanner-bitcode ) were published with a conservative
-- `base <= 4.20` upper bound, which blocks GHC 9.14.1's base-4.22 during
-- dependency resolution. `allow-newer` is scoped to *base only* to keep
-- every other version wall enforced.
--
-- The transitive Hackage ecosystem for GHC 9.14.1 is well-populated by
-- now ( release date : 2026 ) so we don't need per-package relaxations
-- for the wider dep tree here ; if something else surfaces during
-- `cabal build`, add a targeted `<pkg>:<constraint>` line rather than
-- widening `all:` further.

packages: .

allow-newer:
    all:base
